          "path": "_m/g/b/y/x/wellington-clock-tower-wp/swanage-wellington-clock-tower.jpg",
          "filename": "Swanage, Wellington clock tower and pier - geograph.org.uk - 525960.jpg",
          "caption": "Swanage: Wellington clock tower and pier The Wellington clock tower originally stood at the southern end of London Bridge  installed there in 1854 at a cost of £700, it did not keep good time. With increasing traffic, it became something of an obstruction and it was removed to Swanage in 1867. The clock never came. It used to possess a spire but that became unsafe and was removed in 1904.",
